==============================================================================
  6. Indexing and concurrency   (~3 min)
  Syllabus topic: B-tree / expression indexes, query plans, WAL, locking
==============================================================================
  SAY:
   - The bot asks for its latest 200 candles by IST time. The views expose ts AT TIME ZONE 'Asia/Kolkata',
   - so a plain index on ts can't be used. An expression index on that same expression can (D63).

  > EXPLAIN ANALYZE with the expression index
    with candles_ist_ts: Execution Time: 2.680 ms
      ->  Index Scan using instruments_symbol_key on instruments i (actual time=0.020..0.021 rows=1 loops=1)
      ->  Index Scan using candles_ist_ts on candles c (actual time=0.122..0.279 rows=375 loops=1)
      ->  Index Scan using candle_indicators_pkey on candle_indicators ci (actual time=0.003..0.003 rows=1 loops=375)

  > Same query with the index dropped, inside a transaction we roll back (DDL is transactional)
    without the index: Execution Time: 22.750 ms
      ->  Seq Scan on instruments i (actual time=0.024..0.027 rows=1 loops=1)
      ->  Seq Scan on candles c (actual time=17.240..19.249 rows=375 loops=1)
      ->  Index Scan using candle_indicators_pkey on candle_indicators ci (actual time=0.005..0.005 rows=1 loops=375)
    22.75 ms -> 2.68 ms. Index restored by the rollback: True
  [Enter = next step]
  SAY:
   - SQLite: in rollback-journal mode a reader blocks the writer. WAL lets the bot write while we read.

